#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092217 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given in Polar Coordinates"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092218 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87f80908-037b-56ae-a2b5-59bdc49f0acb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given a Description of the Radius and Angle"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad049d53-af38-5917-b9d0-be965cadabcb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given Some Information About Another Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "386a4f1a-4ee5-5bf7-aff2-e190c83f4529" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Using a Diagram"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093428 :tutorial/content "Suppose we know the position of a point $P(r, \\theta)$ in polar coordinates, and we want to convert it into Cartesian coordinates.\n\nTo do this, we can draw a right triangle with legs $x$ and $y$ and hypotenuse $r.$\n\n![](images/20/205b3684042b0ab0261a4d56800cd89a10a7816f8022befcf6c664337f834380.png)\n\nComputing the trigonometric ratios for the triangle above and solving for $x$ and $y,$ we get the following formulas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x}{r}\\, & ⇒ & \\, & x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{y}{r}\\, & ⇒ & \\, & y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use these formulas to write the point $P(2, 60^\\circ)$ in Cartesian coordinates. Here, we have $r=2$ and $\\theta =60^\\circ.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=1, \\\\ y & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P$ can be written in Cartesian coordinates as $P(1, \\sqrt{3}).$" :tutorial/id #uuid "0c11e98f-8b92-5ed1-bfd7-cca35a6dd373" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3505 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
